# Four independent habits in one query: four errors, and applying the fixes gives a program that parses.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv'
| where customerId = "c-001" && amount <> 0
| render columnchart
| take 10
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..88
  PIPELINE@0..87
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 "\n"
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..56
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      BIN_EXPR@21..56
        BIN_EXPR@21..41
          NAME_REF@21..31
            IDENT@21..31 "customerId"
          WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
          EQ@32..33 "="
          WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
          LITERAL@34..41
            STRING@34..41 "\"c-001\""
        WHITESPACE@41..42 " "
        AMP2@42..44 "&&"
        WHITESPACE@44..45 " "
        BIN_EXPR@45..56
          NAME_REF@45..51
            IDENT@45..51 "amount"
          WHITESPACE@51..52 " "
          LTGT@52..54 "<>"
          WHITESPACE@54..55 " "
          LITERAL@55..56
            LONG@55..56 "0"
    WHITESPACE@56..57 "\n"
    PIPE@57..58 "|"
    WHITESPACE@58..59 " "
    RENDER_OP@59..77
      IDENT@59..65 "render"
      WHITESPACE@65..66 " "
      IDENT@66..77 "columnchart"
    WHITESPACE@77..78 "\n"
    PIPE@78..79 "|"
    WHITESPACE@79..80 " "
    TAKE_OP@80..87
      IDENT@80..84 "take"
      WHITESPACE@84..85 " "
      LITERAL@85..87
        LONG@85..87 "10"
  WHITESPACE@87..88 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `=` is assignment, not comparison
  --> query:2:20
  |
2 | | where customerId = "c-001" && amount <> 0
  |                    ^ assignment is not allowed here
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `customerId == "c-001"`

error[DS0111]: `&&` is not an operator
  --> query:2:30
  |
2 | | where customerId = "c-001" && amount <> 0
  |                              ^^
  |
  = help: use `and` to require both conditions

error[DS0107]: `<>` is not an operator
  --> query:2:40
  |
2 | | where customerId = "c-001" && amount <> 0
  |                                        ^^ this is SQL's "not equal"
  |
  = help: use `!=` to test that values differ: `amount != 0`

error[DS0120]: `render` must be the last operator
  --> query:3:3
  |
3 | | render columnchart
  |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
4 | | take 10
  |   ------- this operator comes after `render`
  |
  = help: move `render columnchart` to the end of the query

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv'
    | where customerId == "c-001" and amount != 0
    | take 10
    | render columnchart
which parses without errors
